### =====================================================================
### appointMe - requests.http  (Days 5-11)
### Works with the ids created by scripts/dev-seed.sql
### RUN L1 (LOGIN) FIRST: it stores the token every other request sends.
### Tokens expire (30 min): if you suddenly get 401s, run L1 again.
### "EXPECT" tells you the status you should see.
### =====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### --- Ids from dev-seed.sql -------------------------------------------
@tenantId = 1
@otherTenantId = 2
@serviceId = 1
@service2Id = 2
@otherServiceId = 3
@customerId = 1
@otherCustomerId = 3
@staffId = 2
@otherStaffId = 3


### ======================================================================
### AUTH  (Days 10-11)
### ======================================================================

### L1. LOGIN as Alice (seeded user). EXPECT 200 with accessToken; stores {{token}}
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@test.com", "password": "correct-horse-1" }

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.accessToken); %}

### L2. Wrong password. EXPECT 401 "Invalid email or password"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@test.com", "password": "wrong-password" }

### L3. Unknown email. EXPECT 401, body IDENTICAL to L2 (apart from timestamp)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nobody@example.com", "password": "whatever123" }

### L4. Login is case-insensitive on email. EXPECT 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "  ALICE@TEST.COM ", "password": "correct-horse-1" }

### L5. Missing fields. EXPECT 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### R1. Register. EXPECT 201, no password/hash in the response (run once; rerun gives 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "Test1@Example.com", "password": "correct-horse-1", "fullName": "Test One" }

### R2. Duplicate email, other capitals. EXPECT 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "TEST1@example.com", "password": "correct-horse-1", "fullName": "Clone" }

### R3. Password too short. EXPECT 400, errors.password
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "short@example.com", "password": "abc", "fullName": "Shorty" }

### R4. Bad email + blank name. EXPECT 400, errors for email and fullName
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nope", "password": "correct-horse-1", "fullName": "" }

### ----------------------------------------------------------------------
### TOKEN CHECKS (Day 11). These deliberately use odd Authorization headers.
### ----------------------------------------------------------------------

### J1. Who am I? EXPECT 200, Alice's user object (read from the token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### J2. No token at all. EXPECT 401 (JSON body, WWW-Authenticate: Bearer)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}

### J3. Garbage token. EXPECT 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer this.is.not-a-token

### J4. Wrong scheme (Basic instead of Bearer). EXPECT 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}
Authorization: Basic YWxpY2U6cGFzcw==

### J5. Unsigned "alg":"none" token claiming to be user 1. EXPECT 401
###     (the classic forgery attempt: your decoder is pinned to HS256 and refuses it)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJub25lIn0.eyJzdWIiOiIxIn0.

### J6. TAMPERED token. Run L1, copy the token from the response, then paste it
###     below after changing ONE character in the middle (payload) section.
###     EXPECT 401 (signature no longer matches)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer PASTE.TAMPERED.TOKEN.HERE

### J7. Public endpoints stay public. EXPECT 401 for login-less GET but register/login work (see R1/L1)

### ======================================================================
### TENANTS
### ======================================================================

### T1. Get tenant. EXPECT 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### T2. Create tenant. EXPECT 201 (run once; a second run gives 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Fresh Salon", "slug": "fresh-salon", "timezone": "Europe/Athens" }

### T3. Missing tenant. EXPECT 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/9999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### T4. Duplicate slug. EXPECT 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Copy", "slug": "test-barber", "timezone": "UTC" }

### T5. Bad slug (capitals/space). EXPECT 400 with errors.slug
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Bad Slug", "slug": "Test Barber", "timezone": "UTC" }

### T6. Blank name. EXPECT 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "slug": "no-name", "timezone": "UTC" }

### T7. Unknown time zone. EXPECT 400 "Unknown time zone"
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Mars Barber", "slug": "mars-barber", "timezone": "Mars/Base" }

### T8. Sneaky id in body. EXPECT 201, id is NOT 99
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "id": 99, "name": "Sneaky", "slug": "sneaky", "timezone": "UTC" }

### T9. Empty body. EXPECT 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### T10. No Content-Type header. EXPECT 415
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{"name":"x","slug":"x"}


### ======================================================================
### SERVICES
### ======================================================================

### S1. Create service. EXPECT 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Shave", "durationMinutes": 20, "price": 12.50 }

### S2. Blank name. EXPECT 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "durationMinutes": 30, "price": 25.00 }

### S3. Negative duration. EXPECT 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Haircut", "durationMinutes": -5, "price": 25.00 }

### S4. Missing price. EXPECT 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Haircut", "durationMinutes": 30 }

### S5. Missing duration. EXPECT 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Haircut", "price": 25.00 }

### S6. List. EXPECT 200, tenant 1's services only
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### S7. Get one. EXPECT 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services/{{serviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### S8. Missing service. EXPECT 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services/9999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### S9. Update. EXPECT 200, new price in body
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services/{{serviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Haircut", "durationMinutes": 30, "price": 28.00, "active": true }

### S10. ISOLATION: tenant 2's URL, tenant 1's service. EXPECT 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{otherTenantId}}/services/{{serviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### S11. ISOLATION: update through the wrong tenant. EXPECT 404, data unchanged
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{otherTenantId}}/services/{{serviceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Hacked", "durationMinutes": 1, "price": 0.00, "active": true }

### S12. Soft delete the extra service (Beard Trim). EXPECT 204, row stays with active=false
###      (run dev-seed.sql again afterwards to get it back)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/services/{{service2Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ======================================================================
### CUSTOMERS
### ======================================================================

### C1. Create. EXPECT 201, email saved lowercase
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Cara Lee", "email": "Cara@Example.com", "phone": "6900000010" }

### C2. Duplicate email (different case). EXPECT 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Another Ann", "email": "ANN@example.com" }

### C3. Blank name + bad email. EXPECT 400, errors for fullName and email
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "", "email": "not-an-email" }

### C4. No email. EXPECT 201; run it twice, both succeed
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Walk-in Customer" }

### C5. Search + page + sort. EXPECT 200, only names containing "ann"
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers?name=ann&page=0&size=10&sort=fullName,asc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
### C6. Page 1. EXPECT different rows than page 0

GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers?page=1&size=2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### C7. Size cap. EXPECT "size": 100
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers?size=100000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### C8. Bad sort field. EXPECT 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers?sort=nonsense
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### C9. Get one. EXPECT 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### C10. ISOLATION: tenant 2's URL, tenant 1's customer. EXPECT 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{otherTenantId}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### C11. Update keeping the same email. EXPECT 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Ann Smith-Jones", "email": "ann@example.com", "phone": "6900000099" }

### C12. Update to another customer's email (Ben). EXPECT 409
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/customers/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Ann Smith-Jones", "email": "ben@example.com" }


### ======================================================================
### APPOINTMENTS  (dates must be in the future; today is 2026-10-13)
### ======================================================================

### A1. Create. EXPECT 201, endsAt = startsAt + 30 min (Haircut)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "staffId": {{staffId}},
  "customerId": {{customerId}},
  "serviceId": {{serviceId}},
  "startsAt": "2026-10-20T09:00:00Z",
  "notes": "First visit"
}

### A1b. Second appointment, 15-min service. EXPECT 201, endsAt = 10:15
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "staffId": {{staffId}},
  "customerId": 2,
  "serviceId": {{service2Id}},
  "startsAt": "2026-10-20T10:00:00Z"
}

### A2. In the past. EXPECT 400, errors.startsAt
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": {{staffId}}, "customerId": {{customerId}}, "serviceId": {{serviceId}},
  "startsAt": "2020-01-01T09:00:00Z" }

### A3. Missing fields. EXPECT 400 with several errors
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startsAt": "2026-10-20T11:00:00Z" }

### A4. ATTACK: staff member from another tenant. EXPECT 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": {{otherStaffId}}, "customerId": {{customerId}}, "serviceId": {{serviceId}},
  "startsAt": "2026-10-20T11:00:00Z" }

### A5. ATTACK: customer from another tenant. EXPECT 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": {{staffId}}, "customerId": {{otherCustomerId}}, "serviceId": {{serviceId}},
  "startsAt": "2026-10-20T11:00:00Z" }

### A5b. ATTACK: service from another tenant. EXPECT 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": {{staffId}}, "customerId": {{customerId}}, "serviceId": {{otherServiceId}},
  "startsAt": "2026-10-20T11:00:00Z" }

### A6. Inactive service. EXPECT 400 (run S12 first, which deactivates service 2)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": {{staffId}}, "customerId": {{customerId}}, "serviceId": {{service2Id}},
  "startsAt": "2026-10-20T12:00:00Z" }

### A7. List a range. EXPECT 200, array sorted by startsAt
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/appointments?from=2026-10-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-11-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A8. Range too big. EXPECT 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/appointments?from=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-12-31T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A9. from after to. EXPECT 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/appointments?from=2026-11-01T00:00:00Z&to=2026-10-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### A10. Mark appointment 1 completed. EXPECT 200, status COMPLETED
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/appointments/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "COMPLETED" }

### A11. Change it again. EXPECT 409 (COMPLETED is final)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/appointments/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "NO_SHOW" }

### A12. Unknown status value. EXPECT 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{tenantId}}/appointments/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "BANANA" }

### A13. ISOLATION: tenant 2's URL, tenant 1's appointment. EXPECT 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/tenants/{{otherTenantId}}/appointments/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
